  /*
    COLLAPSED CLIPS THE PANEL. IT MUST NOT `display: none` IT.

    Spotify's embed lives in here, and a display:none iframe is taken out of the
    rendering tree: the browser suspends it, so it stops emitting the regular
    playback_update events this player reads the track position from, and a
    play() issued while it is hidden does not take.

    That caused a real bug, and it only ever reproduced while minimised. The
    end-of-track test fires when position reaches duration, and the swap used to
    be guarded by a 400ms timer. With the iframe suspended, the new track had
    not started when that timer expired, so the embed was still reporting the
    OUTGOING track's position, still past the end: the test passed a second time
    and advanced again. One song skipped, and no sound, because the play() had
    landed on a suspended frame. The guard in the script is now state-based
    rather than timed, which fixes the double advance on its own, but the frame
    still has to stay rendered for playback to survive being minimised at all.

    Clipping keeps the iframe laid out at its real size and merely out of sight,
    which browsers do not suspend. `inert` is applied in the script alongside
    this, because a clipped control is still focusable and a tab stop you cannot
    see is worse than one you can.
